I now have sufficient evidence to render a verdict. Let me compile the assessment.

**Summary of research findings:**
- arXiv:2605.01647, 2604.08554, 2407.12034, Strong Model Collapse ICLR 2025: all verified as real, containing what is claimed
- Qwen3-0.6B: verified available on HuggingFace
- EMNLP 2026 ARR deadline May 25: confirmed
- No competing work on ordinal generational depth scoring found — novelty claim holds
- **Gap found**: arXiv:2502.15654 "Machine-generated text detection prevents language model collapse" (Feb 2025, UCL) uses **binary** DeBERTa-v3 + importance resampling to prevent collapse — the closest upstream related work, not cited anywhere in the proposal
- Round 3 issues: both fully addressed (secondary null + n-gram modeling gap acknowledgment)

